          "id": "8da7667a7815acda948c78db006ce6c429586834",
          "message": "bench: stop spilling before insert-benchmark queries\n\nThe insert benchmark's load.sql called bm25_spill_index() right\nbefore the query phase so that pg_relation_size would reflect the\nfull index footprint.  Side-effect: the queries that follow never\nexercised the in-flight memtable / cache — they ran entirely\nagainst on-disk segments — which made the new cache invisible to\nthis benchmark and undersold what it actually does for\nload-then-query workloads.\n\nMove the spill + size + segment-stats blocks into a new\nsize_report.sql that runs AFTER queries.sql.  The query phase now\nhits the realistic post-load state (chain + cache + segments);\nsize metrics are still captured (just at the very end of the\nstep), so the existing INDEX_SIZE: / TABLE_SIZE: log greps in\nextract_metrics.sh continue to work.\n\nAlso add a benchmark_suite workflow_dispatch input so a single\nsuite (e.g. insert) can be re-run without burning CI minutes on\nthe other three.\n\nCo-authored-by: Copilot <223556219+Copilot@users.noreply.github.com>",
