          "id": "b928eff7fb254f20d6ab0ba46b0af2609a127232",
          "message": "fix: add CHECK_FOR_INTERRUPTS to seek_term_to_doc block-advancing loop\n\nAddresses Claude's PR #360 review nit: the new for(;;) block-\nadvancing loop calls tp_segment_posting_iterator_load_block (disk I/O\n+ possibly decompression) per iteration. Under the cache-\ninconsistency scenario this PR defends against, the loop can iterate\nacross many blocks. Without CFI, statement_timeout / pg_cancel_backend\ncannot abort the scan, and seek_to_pivot's CHECK_FOR_INTERRUPTS one\nlevel up never fires because we never return from seek_term_to_doc.\n\nCo-authored-by: Copilot <223556219+Copilot@users.noreply.github.com>",
