          "id": "831a896e8b1fddde2b0b2aff0c525f2db10c60f7",
          "message": "ci(benchmark): wikipedia validate by per-rank score, not per-doc set\n\nPort the per-rank score validation approach from msmarco\n(#366) to the Wikipedia validator. Run 25745376667 failed\nWikipedia validation with 19 doc-set tie-cluster false\npositives plus 1 real score divergence; the new gate\neliminates the tie-cluster class while still catching real\nper-rank score regressions.\n\nThe two scripts are now structurally aligned: the inner\nLIMIT 10 is held inside the subquery so it propagates to\nthe BM25 index scan (BMW K=10, see #365), the 0.001\nabsolute tolerance is shared, and the allowlist mechanism\nis identical. Doc-set differences are still reported as\nsupplementary info but no longer enter the pass/fail\ndecision.\n\nAllowlist starts empty for Wikipedia. If the lone\nscore-divergence query from run 25745376667 re-surfaces\nunder the new 0.001 tolerance, it can be triaged and\nallowlisted with a tracking issue.\n\nNote: benchmarks/datasets/msmarco-v2/validate_queries.sql\nhas the same legacy doc-set logic and should likely be\nported too; left out of this change to keep the diff\nfocused on what failed on run 25745376667.\n\nCo-authored-by: Copilot <223556219+Copilot@users.noreply.github.com>",
