          "id": "5bd3a2736d0228abc57f72e4f17f464cdb06f3d7",
          "message": "TpVector decode: skip per-record validate + fuse decode/advance\n\nTwo surgical optimizations to the hot read path on the on-disk\nmemtable chain (issue #374), discovered via profiling after the\nquery-term HTAB filter (commit f1e82521) cleared dynahash out of\nthe top of the stack.\n\n1) Skip per-record `tpvector_validate_v2_buffer` on the chain\n   read path.\n\n   The validate function walks every entry's varints purely to\n   bounds-check, which is the same work the ingest pass itself\n   does.  The bytes come from chain pages we wrote ourselves via\n   tp_add_document_terms → create_tpvector_from_strings; the v2\n   buffer was assembled in-process and never crosses a trust\n   boundary on the way to the reader.  Disk-level corruption is\n   caught by the PG buffer manager's page CRC; structural\n   corruption of our own write would point at a bug, not at\n   untrusted input.\n\n   Gate the validate on USE_ASSERT_CHECKING so debug builds keep\n   the cross-check while production builds avoid the redundant\n   varint walk.  Operator-entry-point validators\n   (tpvector_canonicalize, called from recv/out/eq) and the spill\n   path are unchanged — they remain the trust boundary for\n   externally-sourced bytes.\n\n2) Fuse entry decode + advance into one varint pass.\n\n   The legacy iteration pattern\n\n       tpvector_entry_decode(e, &v);   // decode freq + lex_len\n       ...use v...\n       e = get_tpvector_next_entry(e); // re-decode both varints\n                                       //   solely to advance\n\n   re-decoded both varints just to compute the next cursor, even\n   though the first decode had already advanced past them and\n   recorded `v.lexeme + v.lexeme_len`.  For a 30k-record / 30-\n   term-per-record workload this is 1.8M unnecessary varint\n   decode loops per query.\n\n   Add tpvector_entry_decode_advance(entry, &v) → next, which\n   returns `(uint8 *)v.lexeme + v.lexeme_len` (the cursor the\n   varint loop already produced) and update all three in-loop\n   callers — chain_source's ingest_terms, memtable scan's query-\n   vector parse, and build.c's insert path.  The legacy\n   tpvector_entry_decode / get_tpvector_next_entry helpers stay\n   for callers that need either operation independently (output\n   formatting, equality).\n\nMeasured impact on a 30k-doc / 960-page chain (msmarco passages,\ndefault GUCs except memtable_pages_threshold=100000):\n\n  Query                         Before    After    Δ\n  'quantum' (1 term)             60 ms    41 ms   -32%\n  'cancer treatment' (2 terms)   67 ms    59 ms   -12%\n  4 readers, solo bench         61 ms    47 ms   -23%\n\nCumulative speedup from baseline (commit 118ff1ef → this commit)\nincluding the prior query-term filter:\n\n  'quantum'                     60 ms → 41 ms  (1.5×)\n  'cancer treatment'           187 ms → 59 ms  (3.2×)\n\nVerification: make installcheck 64/64 pass; make format-check clean.\n\nCo-authored-by: Copilot <223556219+Copilot@users.noreply.github.com>",
