          "id": "8d4dd21fbbf02018cd7f1943026081ccb10c091d",
          "message": "docs/comments: drop phase-numbered language now the cache work is done\n\nThe in-memory memtable cache implementation landed across a series\nof phases (see prior commit history on this branch); references to\n\"Phase N\" / \"Phase NB\" in comments, SQL scaffolds, test\nheaders, and the design doc no longer carry useful information now\nthat the whole thing is in. Rewrite to descriptive present-tense,\nkeep issue references (#374, #391). The numbered `## Phases`\nsection in docs/memtable_cache.md is replaced with a flat\n`## Scope delivered` summary that lists what was built without\nphase numbers.\n\nOperational/runtime phase markers are unchanged: parallel-build\ncoordination (`phase1_done` / `phase2_cv`), PG progress-reporting\ntokens (`TP_PHASE_LOADING` etc.), `tp_buildphasename`, and\nvacuum.c's algorithmic four-phase approach.\n\nPure documentation/comment cleanup; no behavior change.\n\nCo-authored-by: Copilot <223556219+Copilot@users.noreply.github.com>",
